        {
          "id": "krea2-aeacf191ad2780c4e7a0a619",
          "alias": "单女米衬衫城市站立注视",
          "prompt": "A woman stands by the railway tracks, wearing a beige high-neck long-sleeve shirt with natural wrinkles and textures, presenting a vintage and simple texture that adds a touch of laziness and casualness. She wears a brown plaid newsboy hat, with a black belt pressed down under the brim. The metal buttons on the hat reflect gently in soft light, making it look delicate and detailed. She stands sideways, her overall posture natural relaxed, as if waiting for or just finishing a journey. Her left hand holds a paper bag, Inside the bag were two golden baguettes, the surface crispy and cracks clearly visible. Beside it was a newspaper, its edges slightly curled, printed with blurred text and patterns, hinting at everyday urban life. In the foreground, the rails stretched diagonally from the lower left corner into the distance, their metallic texture reflecting a faint sheen in the sunlight. On both sides of the tracks was a roadbed paved with gravel, varying shades that added layers to the ground. In the middle shot, the background was rendered blurred. Faintly visible white walls and some blurred architectural structures, possibly stations or abandoned industrial facilities. The walls bear mottled marks and fine cracks, revealing the marks of time. Light comes from the upper right, with warm golden sunlight shining on the figures, creating soft outline glows. At the same time, a faint shadow is cast on the left side of the body, enhancing the sense of depth. The transition of light and shadow is natural, creating a tranquil and slightly nostalgic atmosphere. The entire shot uses a shallow depth of field technique, with the focus on the subject, and the background gradually blurring. While highlighting the main subject, it also strengthens the sense of space. The composition uses the rule of thirds: the figure is positioned on the right side of the painting, leaving a large space on the left for the tracks to extend and guide the gaze into the distance. The visual guide is formed by the lines of the tracks and the postures of the figures, from the tracks in the foreground to the figures in the center, then to the blurred buildings in the background, forming a clear visual path. The colors are mainly warm tones, interwoven with beige, brown, orange-yellow, and pale gold, creating a gentle, tranquil, and story-rich atmosphere. The overall style blends the texture of vintage film photography with the poetry of everyday life, as if captured with an old-fashioned camera, full of the atmosphere of life and emotional warmth. The images are delicate and authentic, with rich details—from the texture of clothing to the burnt marks on bread, demonstrating a high degree of realism and artistic expression",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
          "created_at": "2026-09-17T13:54:20.693554",
