        {
          "id": "krea2-ab9d3d875a547ac4751077b6",
          "alias": "单女灰毛衣高塔站立侧头",
          "prompt": "A woman stands on a city pedestrian bridge or viewing platform, wearing a loose light gray coarse knit sweater. The sweater has a clear ribbed texture and natural drape. The shoulders slide slightly to form an exposed shoulder design, revealing one shoulder and collarbone line. Fingers naturally overlap behind the head, posture relaxed and expressive, head slightly tilted, expression calm and content, as if enjoying sunlight and breeze, with a natural sheen and a slightly rosy healthy glow. In the foreground is a white metal railing made of vertical slender columns Neatly arranged, with a slight reflection on the surface, located at the lower edge of the frame, forming a visual framework. The middle ground features a female subject, occupying the center to the right, with her body slightly tilted, arms naturally extended and leaning against the railing. The composition uses a low-angle upward shot to highlight the figure's lines and the vastness of the sky. The background is a blurred cluster of city buildings, with skyscrapers blurred outlines in a grayish-white tone, forming a strong contrast with the deep blue sky. The sky occupies most of the composition, presenting a pure blue-blue with no clouds. The colors are highly saturated, full of summer atmosphere. The overall lighting and shadows are intense daytime natural light, with sunlight shining from above and sides, creating soft shadows and highlights. The sweater's texture is clearly visible under the light, with natural transitions in the shadows. The atmosphere is bright, fresh, warm, and healing. The main tones of the images are blue and gray-white, creating a tranquil, comfortable, and pleasant urban afternoon scene. It has the authentic texture and livelihood of everyday shooting, as if you could casually capture those moments with a regular camera on a sunny day. The lens is slightly overexposed to create a soft halo effect, and the overall style leans toward a blend of documentary photography and fashionable portraits, conveying themes of youth, freedom, and the longing for a better life",
