        {
          "id": "krea2-e7b9cb9ba18db9a04ad3a692",
          "alias": "单女湿身上衣城市困倦注视",
          "prompt": "It has a glossy finish, giving a texture reminiscent of someone just emerging from rain or soaked in moisture, with a slight blush revealing a thoughtful expression. The design cleverly blends traditional and modern elements. She wears a blue knit top decorated with brown Chinese-style frog buttons at the neckline. The lines are simple yet rich in Eastern charm. The fabric is soft and fitted, with visible knit textures in the details. The background is completely blurred, presenting soft light spots of light blue, pale pink, and gray-green, creating a dreamy bokeh effect. The composition uses the classic rule of thirds: the figure is on the right side of the frame, leaving plenty of negative space on the left, guiding the gaze into the distance, creating a strong visual direction. The light comes from the upper left of the image, soft natural light, like the slanting sun in the morning or evening, forming a warm backlit silhouette. The shadows transition naturally, with rich layers and subtle contrasts of light and shadow. The overall atmosphere is tranquil and poetic, tinged with a hint of melancholy and nostalgia, as if capturing a moment of contemplation. The image has a strong film-like texture, moderate color saturation, a slight retro filter effect, and a slight graininess, resembling real images taken with an old camera. The lens uses a large-aperture prime lens with a focal length of about 85mm, extremely shallow depth of field, a completely blurred background, and a sharp subject The images present a realistic feel reminiscent of everyday amateur equipment shooting, without excessive embellishment, preserving the original light and texture. The overall style combines fashion and artistry, combining the sophistication of modern urban beauty with traditional cultural symbols, creating a unique and thought-provoking visual experience",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
