        {
          "id": "krea2-8dd447656d406894d14bf5ef",
          "alias": "单女红衬衫摄影棚忧伤坐侧头",
          "prompt": "A woman sits in the back seat of an old car, leaning sideways against the window, her head slightly tilted, her expression slightly melancholic and contemplative, as if whispering softly or just ending a conversation. She wears a loose red and white striped shirt with rolled-up cuffs, revealing slender arms. She seems to be holding a vague little object, possibly a phone or keys. Her leg is covered with a colorful printed fabric featuring cartoon characters and graffiti-style patterns, full of childlike fun and vintage charm. The foreground shows the metal window frame of a car, with some worn and rusted edges, showing signs of time. The window glass reflects a blurred indoor scene, including a wooden table, several chairs, and some stacked books and miscellaneous items. In the background, a faint red circular object can be seen, resembling an old radio or decorative item. The entire scene is set in a messy yet cozy indoor space, possibly a studio or a family living room, with light slanting in from the right, creating a soft backlight effect. Creating a warm and hazy atmosphere, the composition uses close-ups, placing the person on the right side of the frame and leaving ample space on the left to show the environment inside and outside the window, creating visual balance and contrast. The camera angle is slightly tilted, enhancing a casual and documentary feel, as if captured casually with an old film camera. The light and shadow layers are rich, highlights are bright but not overexposed, shadows transition delicately, and the overall tone is warm, with slight graininess and low color saturation. It simulates the unique texture of film photography, with no obvious post-processing marks in the images, preserving the roughness and realism of the original shots, giving a nostalgic, quiet, and story-rich everyday visual experience",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
