        {
          "id": "krea2-a1ad52b2b25ede0a8a601c93",
          "alias": "单女和服花园温柔坐注视",
          "prompt": "A woman dressed in traditional kimono sits sideways on the tatami floor of a traditional Japanese building. Her figure is outlined by the soft natural light streaming through the window, her silhouette outlined in a high bun. She slightly lowers her head and gazes at a single pink flower in her hand. The slender stems and leaves and tender green leaves shimmer with a crystal-clear texture in the light. The petals bloom lightly, as if carrying a silent longing or sense of ritual. Her hands gently cupped the flower, her movements gentle and focused, her sleeves hanging wide, The fabric is delicately folded, forming natural layers of light and shadow with the posture of the body. The overall composition adopts a classic center-offset layout, with the figure positioned on the left side of the painting, leaving a large negative space on the right, creating an ethereal and tranquil Eastern aesthetic atmosphere. The foreground features a dark wooden floor with clear grain and a gentle texture shaped by the passage of time. The floor surface reflects faint light, enhancing the sense of realism and depth of the space. The middle ground depicts the female subject and her environment, including the paper sliding door (shoji screen) behind her. Its grid-like structure presents a semi-transparent warm white tone under the backlight, emitting soft diffused light that makes the entire interior feel tranquil and warm. The background is the outdoor scene seen through the glass window, with blurred green vegetation and scattered pink branches intertwining to create a hazy natural scene. Distant tree branches intertwine, creating a blurred layering that enhances depth of field and spatial depth. In composition, windows are used as natural frames, placing figures within the frame and creating strong visual guidance. The viewer's gaze naturally focuses on the figure and the flower in their hand, while the contrast of light and shadow emphasizes the dramatic tension between light and shadow. The light mainly comes from outside, creating a backlit effect that makes the figures silhouettes and create subtle transitions. This treatment of light and shadow gives the painting a poetic sense of calm. The overall atmosphere is tranquil, introspective, and full of Zen spirit, like a momentary moment frozen in a Japanese garden afternoon. The tones are dominated by black, white, and gray, accented with pale pink flowers and tender green leaves, with restrained yet emotionally rich colors. The image presents a texture similar to medium format film photography, with slight graininess and a soft dynamic range. The exposure is slightly underexposed, preserving details in dark areas while highlighting transparency in bright areas. The lens is a 50mm standard prime lens, with a viewpoint straight ahead, close to the ground, enhancing immersion and realism. The overall style blends the characteristics of documentary photography and artistic portraiture, serving both as a private record of daily life and as a carefully crafted still life portrait, conveying a profound philosophical reflection on time, memory, and beauty There are no unnecessary decorations in the painting; all elements serve the pure expression of the theme, ultimately presenting a tranquil beauty that transcends reality, allowing one to feel the profound understanding of the beauty of \"wabi-sabi\" in Eastern culture.",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
          "created_at": "2026-09-17T13:54:20.693554",
