        {
          "id": "krea2-e1c45ffdab7c20ddbbc1a29e",
          "alias": "单女白T恤车内倚靠注视",
          "prompt": "She wore an off-white loose short-sleeved T-shirt, the hem casually tucked into her waistband, revealing her slender waist and abdominal line. She paired it with high-waisted white denim shorts with slight trimming at the legs, leaving her feet bare, feet naturally hanging inside the car, left leg bent, right leg extended, body slightly leaning forward She grips the steering wheel with both hands, left hand on top, right hand below, fingers long, posture relaxed and dynamic. She wears a thin chain necklace around her neck, a small and delicate pendant, and seems to be wearing a simple wristband on her wrist. The overall look is casual yet fashionable, full of youthful energy. The sports car's body is bright red all over, with a smooth, mirror-like paint that reflects the surrounding light and shadow. The doors are open, the interior is made of black genuine leather, the seats are wide and comfortable, the headrest and side wings are well wrapped, and there is a purple decoration in the center of the steering wheel. It may be a modification or accessory. The rear features a large carbon fiber rear wing with a streamlined design and subtle textures. The wheels are multi-spoke in color in bronze or deep gold, and the tires have a low aspect ratio, showing high performance. The windows are transparent, allowing you to see interior details. The inside of the doors has handles and control buttons, and the roof is a foldable soft top, currently folded. The car is parked on a narrow street with gray cement with slight wear and tear. The background is a typical Japanese-style residence. The exterior walls are made of light gray horizontal wood panels with a delicate texture. The window frames are deep red, with white curtains hanging inside, letting in soft light. On the left is a deep reddish-brown wooden door with two round metal door rings. Above the door is a house number \"68\". The roof is a traditional tiled structure in deep gray-blue, with slightly raised eaves, showcasing a strong Japanese architectural style. In front of the door are low stone steps and brick walls, with a small amount of moss growing in the corners. On the right, you can see part of the wall and ventilation shaft of another building. The overall lighting is natural light, usually in the afternoon. Sunlight pours in from the upper right of the frame, casting soft shadows on the characters and vehicles. The sky is pale blue, clouds thin, and green vegetation faintly visible in the distance. The composition uses a medium perspective: the figure is positioned slightly to the right, the sports car occupies the lower left to the center, forming the visual center. The foreground focuses on the edges of sports car doors, hoods, and wheels; the middle ground is the main part of the people and interior; the background features residential buildings and street environments. Visual guidance is created through the figures' postures and gaze directions, as well as the lines of the sports car, creating a sense of dynamic balance. The lighting atmosphere is warm and realistic, with vivid color contrasts. The red body contrasts strongly with light-colored clothing and background buildings, while the soft lighting maintains harmony. The overall composition presents a fleeting beauty from everyday life, unexpectedly presented. It feels as if you were shooting with an amateur camera, preserving authentic texture and the atmosphere of life. The tone leans slightly toward warmth, with slight graininess and noise, simulating film photography effects and enhancing the retro and nostalgic atmosphere of the images. The rich details and clarity of architectural textures all reflect a high degree of realism and artistic expression. The overall style blends street culture, car culture, and youthful aesthetics, creating a free, individualistic, and vibrant lifestyle attitude",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
