        {
          "id": "krea2-96ab6a195b9aa5b159ef7e49",
          "alias": "单女灰毛衣客厅愤怒倚靠注视",
          "prompt": "A woman leans half out from behind a black metal-framed chair, staring directly at the camera, as if she is about to speak softly or has just secretly glimpsed something interesting. Her hands rest lightly on the armrest's crossbar, her nails neatly trimmed and painted a pale pink nail polish. She wears a soft-textured light gray ribbed knit sweater, with the cuffs slightly rolled up to reveal the skin on her wrist. The composition uses a low-angle downward view, giving viewers a subtle sense of pressure and intimacy as if she is \"watching,\" while also reinforcing the presence of the main subject. In the background is a wooden-floored corridor leading deep inside, covered with a wide striped carpet in beige, light gray, and pale yellow, with slightly worn edges, revealing a sense of life; At the end of the corridor is an old vermilion wooden door, with round brass ring handles and intricate traditional carved decorations on the door panel. The edges of the door frame are slightly mottled, exuding a strong Eastern classical charm; Beside the right wall hangs a drooping green vine plant, its leaves dense and soft, creating a hazy blur effect under soft light, creating a contrast in color and texture with the pristine white wall on the left. The overall composition uses a shallow depth of field technique, with background elements such as red doors, greenery, and corridor spaces moderately blurred to create a sense of spatial depth with clear layers. Light scatters from the window in the upper left, soft but not glaring, creating a delicate transition between light and shadow, while leaving slight shadows behind her and on the seat back, enhancing the sense of depth. The atmosphere is tranquil yet poetic, carrying a touch of nostalgic artistic flair and the warmth of everyday life. It's like capturing a moment when the afternoon sunlight slants into the living room of an old house—both real and dreamy, both innocent and lively, yet subtly expressing a desire to explore the unknown. The tone leans toward warm gray tones with moderate saturation, emphasizing the authenticity of the material texture—the velvety feel of sweaters, the cold hardness of metal chair frames, the warmth of wooden floors, the heaviness of the red door lacquer, and the delicate veins of green plants. The visual guide extends from the foreground chair back to the middle ground carpet, heading toward the red door in the background, forming a stable spatial axis. The tilted posture of the woman's head disrupts vertical balance, increasing dynamic tension. The entire image looks as if taken with an amateur camera (such as the Sony A6000 series or Canon M50) in natural indoor light, with slight noise and film graininess, retaining the graininess and slight color shift of the original RAW file, making the image more realistic and lifelike rather than an overly polished commercial style. It conveys a kind of \"beauty that is unintentionally frozen in time\"—not deliberately staged perfection, but gentle moments quietly occurring in ordinary days, making one want to step into this space and listen to the story behind it.",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
