        {
          "id": "krea2-3d35285d95e15aaedf81a203",
          "alias": "单女长裤车厢忧伤注视",
          "prompt": "In the center of the train station, with its black-and-white film texture, a woman holds a vintage rangefinder camera facing the camera, steadily holding a classic mechanical camera engraved with the word \"PENTAX\" in both hands, creating a mysterious and focused photographer's posture; She wore a lightweight lace cut-out top with naturally draped cuffs, dark cargo pants at the waist accentuating her slender waistline, and a simple metal watch strap on her wrist, revealing a blend of artistic and practical everyday style; In the foreground, sharp railway tracks extend deep into the frame, with the railroad ties and rough textures forming a strong perspective line that firmly draws the viewer's gaze to the main figure; The middle ground features the edge of the platform and the blurred silhouettes of people, with faintly visible distant waiting passengers or staff blurred to enhance the sense of spatial depth; In the background, the towering platform canopy structure, with interlaced steel frames and long tubes of fluorescent tubes forming soft circular light spots under shallow depth, scattered like stars under the gray-white sky, creating a spatial layer where industrial aesthetics and nostalgic atmosphere intertwine; The composition adopts a centrally symmetrical golden ratio layout, with the figure positioned at the center of the frame, and the tracks on both sides radiating toward the distance, forming a stable anchor point for the visual focal point; In terms of lighting and shadow, the overall environment is cloudy with diffused light and a cool gray tone. The camera's top flash is off, only the top light casts even, soft side backlighting, and the track shadows deepen the sense of depth. The atmosphere is filled with a calm, lonely, yet exploratory mood, as if time has frozen in this moment. It carries a touch of melancholic romanticism and a tribute to mechanical aesthetics, evoking the classic style of street photographers from the 1970s. It combines a documentary power with artistic blank spaces, offering an immersive viewing experience.",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
