        {
          "id": "krea2-16ac1939c34590e05c763680",
          "alias": "单女街道坐持杯",
          "prompt": "In an image filled with the vibrant atmosphere of Vietnamese street life and a literary, retro artistic atmosphere, the subject of the painting is a woman sitting upright in front of an open wooden windowsill in a quaint café, wearing an elegant white traditional top. In her left hand, she gently holds a glass of orange-yellow beverage, with a straw stuck in the rim. On her right hand stands a Vietnamese bamboo hat painted with traditional ink landscape patterns in blue and white, slightly tilted against the wooden railing. As if ready to be picked up at any moment. Beside her is a classic black film camera, with the lens pointed to the right side of the frame, hinting that she may have just pressed the shutter or was about to capture a street scene. The entire windowsill is made of rugged logs, with clearly visible wood grain. Below is a mottled warm yellow wall, where sunlight filters through the vines above, casting fine, rhythmic stripes of light and shadow on the wall.",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
