        {
          "id": "krea2-dd8263588134741e62567881",
          "alias": "多人注视",
          "prompt": "In terms of composition, it uses a four-panel split-screen layout, with each image independent yet unified, constructing a continuous storytelling through different postures and perspectives of the characters. Shots are often shot from low angles or straight ahead, enhancing the subject's presence and spatial depth. Tree branches and leaves are often naturally cut at the edges of the painting, forming a framed composition that enhances the sense of envelopment and immersion. Clear visual guidelines—extending from the foreground flowerbed to the figure's legs, guiding the viewer's gaze naturally and ultimately stopping on the details of the character's expression.",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
